# Integrity manifest for backup-databases.sh
# =============================================================================
#
# This file pins the SHA-256 of the trusted version of
# tools/scripts/database/backup-databases.sh that the scheduled
# production backup workflow is permitted to execute on the droplet.
#
# Without this pin, backup-production.yml checked out HEAD of origin/main,
# meaning any attacker who landed a malicious commit on main would gain
# arbitrary code execution on the droplet as the SSH user during the
# nightly backup job.
#
# # Maintenance contract (INFRA-1 fix, plan v4 W2-E)
#
#   1. Any change to `tools/scripts/database/backup-databases.sh`
#      REQUIRES a paired update to the hash below in the same PR.
#   2. CI enforces the manifest-vs-script match via
#      `.github/workflows/backup-manifest-invariant.yml` (W3) —
#      PR fails if hash drifts from the file content.
#   3. Per BLOCKER-9 CODEOWNERS routing, both the workflow file and
#      this manifest live under `.github/**` which routes to @Okan-wqm.
#      A malicious PR cannot silently update the manifest alongside
#      the script.
#
# # Regenerating the hash
#
#   sha256sum tools/scripts/database/backup-databases.sh
#
# # Refs
#
#   /root/.claude/plans/declarative-riding-shamir.md INFRA-1
#   /var/aqua-saas/docs/reviews/_audit/2026-04-W16-unified-audit.md
#     (infra-expert finding surfacing the git-checkout-of-origin-main
#     code-execution vector)
#
# =============================================================================

# sha256  path
ef9c3857b91f10bfe23f55ed079376e27e03396df25aa63de80bd86ef042beb4  tools/scripts/database/backup-databases.sh
